{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-014",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 14,
  "title": "Job 14",
  "display_title": "Job 14",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 14,
  "sortOrder": 18014,
  "verseCount": 22,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Man that is born of a woman is of few days, and full of trouble.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "He cometh forth like a flower, and is cut down: he fleeth also as a shadow, and continueth not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "And dost thou open thine eyes upon such an one, and bringest me into judgment with thee?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Who can bring a clean thing out of an unclean? not one.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Seeing his days are determined, the number of his months are with thee, thou hast appointed his bounds that he cannot pass;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Turn from him, that he may rest, till he shall accomplish, as an hireling, his day.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "For there is hope of a tree, if it be cut down, that it will sprout again, and that the tender branch thereof will not cease.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Though the root thereof wax old in the earth, and the stock thereof die in the ground;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Yet through the scent of water it will bud, and bring forth boughs like a plant.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But man dieth, and wasteth away: yea, man giveth up the ghost, and where is he?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "As the waters fail from the sea, and the flood decayeth and drieth up:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "So man lieth down, and riseth not: till the heavens be no more, they shall not awake, nor be raised out of their sleep.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "O that thou wouldest hide me in the grave, that thou wouldest keep me secret, until thy wrath be past, that thou wouldest appoint me a set time, and remember me!",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "If a man die, shall he live again? all the days of my appointed time will I wait, till my change come.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Thou shalt call, and I will answer thee: thou wilt have a desire to the work of thine hands.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "For now thou numberest my steps: dost thou not watch over my sin?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "My transgression is sealed up in a bag, and thou sewest up mine iniquity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "And surely the mountain falling cometh to nought, and the rock is removed out of his place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The waters wear the stones: thou washest away the things which grow out of the dust of the earth; and thou destroyest the hope of man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Thou prevailest for ever against him, and he passeth: thou changest his countenance, and sendest him away.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "His sons come to honour, and he knoweth it not; and they are brought low, but he perceiveth it not of them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:14:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "But his flesh upon him shall have pain, and his soul within him shall mourn.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 14:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:14:22"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
